PROJECT: MCP File Server
STATUS: Local implementation working; PM2, health checks, MCP transport probes, and the two-session public HTTPS demonstration verified; GitHub publication still requires completion.

PURPOSE
Provide an AI agent with authenticated MCP tools for managing files inside a restricted workspace.

TECH STACK
- Node.js and TypeScript
- MCP TypeScript SDK
- Express
- Zod
- Streamable HTTP transport

CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION
- Eight original tools plus str_replace (nine total).
- Local HTTP endpoint: http://127.0.0.1:3000/mcp
- Health endpoint: http://127.0.0.1:3000/health
- Bearer-token authentication using MCP_AUTH_TOKEN.
- Workspace root: workspace/
- MCP Inspector CLI connected to the public endpoint and listed all nine tools; discovery is not the same as executing every tool remotely.
- Path traversal attempts were rejected in earlier tests.
- TypeScript check passed using npx.cmd tsc --noEmit.
- Security audit verified locally on 2026-10-15: all nine tools register, traversal and outside-workspace symlink attempts are rejected, and move_file preserves an existing destination.
- Final readiness audit verified on 2026-10-15: PM2 reported `mcp-file-server` online; local and public health endpoints returned HTTP 200. README and implementation documentation were added.
- Verified on 2026-10-15: authenticated local and public MCP sessions initialized with HTTP 200 and session IDs; `create_file` returned HTTP 200 and successful tool results for `reports/local-probe-f5ba9f6499c04bf1a7dae407fbd868eb.txt` and `reports/public-probe-198e2b5a01f947b9945915a673be825b.txt`.
- Verified two-session public HTTPS demonstration on 2026-10-15: Session 1 created `reports/two-session-demo.txt`; independently initialized Session 2 read the exact content with HTTP 200. Sanitized evidence: `workspace/reports/two-session-demo-evidence.md`.

GIT HISTORY
- 33ffc95: feat: add safe exact-text replacement tool
- bf58023: establish working MCP file server baseline

CURRENT LIMITATIONS
- Required handoff files created and verified.
- Intermittent Inspector CLI `fetch failed / other side closed` errors remain unexplained and are not considered fixed.
- Complete remote MCP evidence for all nine tools has not been captured. The verified public calls cover `create_file` and `read_file`; Inspector tool discovery is not remote execution of all nine tools.
- No Git remote was configured during this audit, so public GitHub publication remains pending.
- Filesystem path checks cannot eliminate every time-of-check/time-of-use race if an untrusted local process can modify the workspace concurrently. Keep workspace write access limited to the server account and trusted users.

NEXT PRIORITIES
